# %% [md] 05 -- how H_m sits over T_m: Loewy layers, socle layers, Jordan types.
# module_structure(m) is the LoewyProfile of the block H^1_m over the local algebra T_m. Its Loewy layers
# (the radical filtration) and socle layers are dimensions in units of f; jordan(p) is the Jordan type of
# T_p - a_p on the block. At (10, 691) the block is 3-dimensional with Loewy layers 2 | 1 and Jordan type
# (2, 1): T_p - (1 + p^11) is nilpotent but not zero -- a non-split extension of Eisenstein by cusp.

# %% Setting and the maximal ideal
# The coefficient ring is the default F_ell, stated here so that the file runs in any order in one session (08 sets Z).
set coefficient_ring = "F_ell";
R = ext_record(10, 691);
m = R.ideal(0);

# %% The Loewy profile
P = module_structure(m);
display(P);

# %% The Jordan type of T_2
display(P.jordan(2));
